<title>USA: US FTC member says met with EU's Van Miert.</title>
<headline>US FTC member says met with EU's Van Miert.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Trade Commission member Mary Azcuenaga said she met Thursday with EU Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert in Brussels during a long-planned trip to discuss various issues with EU officials.</p>
<p>In a telephone interview from Brussels, Azcuenaga declined to comment on whether she talked to Van Miert about the proposed Boeing Co -McDonnell Douglas merger.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm not saying it didn't come up,&quot; she said. &quot;I'm not going to deny that it came up, but I'm not going to confirm it either.&quot;</p>
<p>Azcuenaga said she and Van Miert covered a wide range of issues and pending matters during their meeting, which lasted less than an hour.</p>
<p>&quot;It would be wrong to suggest that the purpose of my visit was to discuss the case,&quot; she added.</p>
<p>She said she was also meeting with other EU officials who deal with competition and consumer protection issues.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
